&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Board-Focused Hardware Test &amp;amp; Design Engineer at Neros, you will own the hardware architecture and implementation of manufacturing test solutions used to validate PCBAs and electronic assemblies from prototype builds through high-volume production. This role bridges product design, manufacturing, and test engineering by developing scalable, high-coverage board-level test systems that improve product quality, accelerate root-cause analysis, and enable efficient production ramping.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop board-level manufacturing test hardware, including bed-of-nails and custom fixturing solutions for PCBA validation and production testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with electrical, mechanical, and manufacturing engineering teams to influence product designs for testability (DFT), ensuring adequate test access, coverage, and fault isolation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define board-level test strategies spanning ICT, functional test, programming, calibration, and metrology systems across development and production stages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own hardware design for manufacturing test equipment, including fixture electronics, interface boards, signal conditioning, switching architectures, and measurement systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with contract manufacturers and internal production teams to deploy, qualify, and sustain test solutions at vendor sites and Neros headquarters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze test coverage, yield performance, and failure trends to drive continuous improvements in test effectiveness, throughput, reliability, and overall manufacturing quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should have the following&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in electrical engineering, manufacturing test engineering, hardware validation, or product test development, with ownership of board-level and system-level test solutions from prototype through high-volume production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience developing and deploying PCBA manufacturing test strategies, including ICT, bed-of-nails, flying probe, boundary scan (JTAG), functional test, programming, calibration, and end-of-line validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of electronic circuit design, schematic review, signal integrity, power distribution, analog and digital interfaces, and failure analysis techniques&lt;/li&gt;
