&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Logistics Manager will own all domestic and international shipping operations for controlled and hazardous materials, including lithium batteries, defense-related electronics, and ITAR-restricted items. This individual will be responsible for building and managing logistics systems, ensuring compliance with international trade and export regulations, and developing scalable processes to support production growth and global expansion. This role requires deep expertise in international trade compliance, dangerous goods transportation, and defense export controls, combined with a hands-on approach to execution. The ideal candidate is equally comfortable developing strategic logistics frameworks and managing day-to-day shipping operations.&lt;/p&gt;
