&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of RCCA and structured problem solving (8D, 5 Whys, fishbone), PFMEA, control plans, FAI (AS9102 or similar), and SPC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of IPC/WHMA-A-620 as it applies to cable, harness, and connector workmanship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with brushless motors, including bearings, balancing, winding and lead termination, and common failure modes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of vibration, shock, and thermal effects on assembled hardware and how to design inspections and screens around them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort on the bench with multimeters, power supplies, and basic motor and continuity testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with composites, machining, injection molding, and additive manufacturing processes and their common defect modes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ISO 9001 or AS9100 quality systems in a defense or aerospace environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with drones, RC aircraft, or FPV hardware. If you’ve built quads from a bare frame and tracked down why one kept losing a motor mid-flight, we want to hear about it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
