&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to build a million drones a year here in America, and the production line that builds them needs an embedded quality resource: the specialist. As a Quality Specialist, you will be proficient in inspection, measurement, and quality systems and will be trusted to develop and improve them as well as train others in them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the role that blends the best of both inspector and engineer, resulting in highly skilled hands-on expertise with engineering judgement and authority. You inspect to drawings and procedures, but you also write the inspection plans. You verify production builds, but you also define how a new product gets inspected before anyone has built it. When a defect shows up, you’re the one who contains it, and then you make sure it doesn’t escape the same way twice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’ve spent years on a production floor learning quality inspection and engineering, and you want to build something that matters with high ownership and hands-on engagement, this is your role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform first article, in-process, and final inspections on mechanical, electrical, and PCBA assemblies against drawings, specifications, and workmanship standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure and verify parts and assemblies with precision tools (calipers, micrometers, height and pin gauges, optical comparators, and vision systems) and interpret GD&amp;amp;T on engineering drawings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage non-conforming product on the line, then contain, document, and lead MRB disposition with engineering and production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain inspection plans, verification criteria, checklists, and quality work instructions for new and existing products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support NPI through design and process reviews, PFMEA, and control plan development, establishing inspection points before product hits rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Watch quality data (yield, defect Pareto, escapes, SPC) and flag trends before they become line-down events or field failures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own calibration of inspection and measurement equipment and maintain quality records and traceability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train operators and technicians on inspection criteria, workmanship standards, and quality procedures, and support internal and customer audits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
